# The Borg shader ISA, in the format of riscv-opcodes: a name, its operand fields
# (fields.csv) and the fixed bits. Every bit of a word is an operand or fixed.
# scripts/isa_gen.py generates the Scala decoder constants (mill) and borg_isa.h
# (make rdl) from it at build time; mesa keeps a copy for the compiler's opcodes.rs.
# rv_i and rv_zicsr hold the instructions (ISA v2, docs/B8_isa_v2.md), csrs.csv the CSRs.

# HALT is the all-zero word; major opcodes 0x00 and 0x04 hold no instruction.
$pseudo_op none halt        31..0=0
